-- title:
--   Ordinary local root count one at p ‖ N
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, let $p\neq 2$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional residual Galois representation over $k$ (a $k$-vector space of rank $2$ with a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ into its endomorphisms that is trivial on the absolute Galois group of some number field) whose base change to $\overline{k}$ has no nontrivial stable subspace. Let $S\supseteq S_{\min}$ be finite sets of primes with $p\in S_{\min}$, such that for primes $q\neq p$ one has $q\in S_{\min}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$, and such that for $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$, every inertia element at $q$ acts with characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$. Let $N\neq 0$ satisfy: all prime divisors of $N$ lie in $S$; $p^2\nmid N$; every $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$, divides $N$; every prime $q\neq p$ outside $S_{\min}$ dividing $N$ has $q^2\mid N$; no prime cube divides $N$; and weight-$2$ cusp forms of level $N$ are spanned over $\mathbb C$ by those with integral $q$-coefficients. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra $\mathbb T^S(N)$, the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$) and the $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$), to $k$, such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $P$ and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Assume moreover $p\mid N$ and that $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$: for each valuation subring over $p$ there is a free rank-one summand $L$, spanned by a member of a basis, stable under the decomposition group, with $(\sigma-1)v\in L$ for all $v$ and all inertia elements $\sigma$. Fix $c\in k$, $c\neq 0$; call $x\in\overline{K}:=\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}(\mathrm{Frac}\,\mathcal O)$ residually $c$ if $x$ is a root of some monic $R\in\mathcal O[X]$ whose reduction is $(X-C\,c)^{\deg R}$. For a newform datum $(M_g,g,\chi_g,\iota)$ — $M_g\mid N$, $g$ a weight-$2$ newform on $\Gamma_0(M_g)$ (a normalised eigenform not matching, on primes away from $M_g$, the eigensystem of any normalised eigenform of smaller level dividing $M_g$), $\chi_g:\mathbb T^{\emptyset}(M_g)\to\mathbb C$ sending $T_\ell$ and $U_q$ to the corresponding $q$-coefficients of $g$, and a ring homomorphism $\iota$ from the range of $\chi_g$ to $\overline K$ — write $a_p=\iota(U_p)$ if $p\mid M_g$ and $a_p=\iota(T_p)$ otherwise, $e=v_p(N)-v_p(M_g)$, and let $P$ be $X-a_p$ when $e=0$ and $X^{e-1}(X^2-a_pX+p\,[p\nmid M_g])$ otherwise (guarded in the Lean text by the primality of $p$, which holds). Assume given an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\chi_0$ from the localisation $\mathbb T^S(N)\otimes\mathcal O$ at the complement of $\ker\theta$ to $\overline K$ and an element $a_0\in\overline K$ residually $c$ that is a root of $P$ for every newform datum whose $\iota(T_\ell)$ agree with $\chi_0(T_\ell)$ for all primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$. Then for every $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\chi$ of that localisation into $\overline K$ there is a newform datum $(M_g,g,\chi_g,\iota)$ with $\iota(T_\ell)=\chi(T_\ell)$ for all primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, whose associated polynomial $P$ satisfies: the sum of $\mathrm{rootMultiplicity}_x P$ over the distinct roots $x$ of $P$ that are residually $c$ equals $1$.
--
--   This is the local multiplicity-one count at $p$ in the ordinary case: at a prime $p$ exactly dividing the level, the $U_p$- or $T_p$-factor of the newform datum behind any $\overline K$-point of the localised Hecke algebra contributes exactly one root in the residue class $c$ of the unit root. It is the input for the computation of newform multiplicities as the dimension of the corresponding eigenspace over the algebraic closure, and rests on the uniform unit-root statement [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_ne_zero_forall_algHom_algebraicClosure_isNewform_residual_unitRoot_of_isOrdinaryAt`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_ne_zero_forall_algHom_algebraicClosure_isNewform_residual_unitRoot_of_isOrdinaryAt) together with the uniqueness of the residual value attached to an element of $\overline K$ by a monic polynomial with totally split reduction.
